    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0448" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894A.24/12–649</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Secretary of State for Far
                        Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Butterworth</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1949-12-07">December 7, 1949</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Attached is a memorandum of a conversation<anchor n="66" xml:id="d470-f1"/> with
                    Mr. Graves, Counselor of the British Embassy, which foreshadows what the British
                    Ambassador will say to you tomorrow regarding Formosa. Mr. Graves also left an
                        <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> which is likewise attached.<anchor
                        n="67" xml:id="d470-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Also attached is a memorandum listing the military supplies which remain to be
                    shipped to the Chinese Government on Formosa, some of which have been purchased
                    from the $125 million grants and other items which have been procured by the
                    Chinese with their own funds.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W[<hi rendition="#small-caps">alton</hi>] B[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">utterworth</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d470-a1.xml" xpointer="d470-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
